title: Knock / request-to-join for gated rooms
---
The 4-level room visibility model (public / unlisted / gated / private) names a 'gated' tier = LISTED + invite-gated: a room you can discover via list_rooms but cannot join without an invite. Without a knock / request-to-join flow, 'gated' is a dead-end teaser UX (you see it, can't join, can't ask).

Build a knock mechanism so a non-member who finds a gated room can REQUEST to join: request enqueues to room admins/inviters, who can approve (= issue invite) or deny. Surfaces: relay signed op (knock_room), local broker, MCP tool, CLI (c2c rooms knock <room>), and a way for members to see/approve pending knocks.

NOT building now — placeholder so 'gated' has a path to first-class UX. Until then 'gated' = discoverable but invite-only (invite must be issued out-of-band by a member).